6-08-01 — and my headline was wrong in the best way: the job HAD fired, both days, on schedule.\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"launchd\",\n        \"macos\",\n        \"claude-code\",\n        \"automation\",\n        \"scheduling\"\n      ],\n      \"stack\": null,\n      \"tier\": \"T0\",\n      \"capability\": \"T0 · inert — touches nothing\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"about_tiers\": \"Tier is a CAPABILITY (blast-radius) disclosure, not a safety verdict: higher just means look closer. Run check_capability on the live files before applying a story.\"\n}"}}}
