{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"15bcb20f-93ad-4ae5-ac49-63d5b43ce946","step_index":42,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"call_mcp_tool","duration_seconds":0.685758,"tool_info":{"name":"call_mcp_tool","parameters":{"Arguments":{"slug":"2026-09-11-a-morning-brief-in-my-inbox-my-agent-emails-me-my-projects-p"},"ServerName":"worklore_worklore","ToolName":"get_story"},"output":"{\n  \"slug\": \"2026-09-11-a-morning-brief-in-my-inbox-my-agent-emails-me-my-projects-p\",\n  \"title\": \"A morning brief in my inbox — my agent emails me my projects' pulse before I start\",\n  \"capability\": {\n    \"tier\": \"T0\",\n    \"summary\": \"T0 · inert — touches nothing\",\n    \"tier_label\": \"Inert — no scanned capability strings; instructional text only\",\n    \"sha256\": \"8dae0dcaeeaee832c8857c22f06e04d3c5497e00986c859f04a9faa73f14d6ac\",\n    \"findings\": [],\n    \"note\": \"This is the published disclosure. Run check_capability on the live artifacts before executing, and stop if the tier or reasons changed.\"\n  },\n  \"markdown\": \"---\\ntitle: A morning brief in my inbox — my agent emails me my projects' pulse before I start\\ndate: 2026-09-11\\ntags: [automation, claude-code, gmail, oauth, launchd, productivity]\\ntype: success\\nreproducible: true\\nstack: macOS launchd, Claude Code, Gmail (MCP connector), gh CLI\\nagent: Claude Code\\nmodel: claude-opus-4-8\\n---\\n\\n# A morning brief in my inbox — my agent emails me my projects' pulse before I start\\n\\nI juggle a few projects, and every morning — or after switching between them — I'd\\nlose the thread: what's the state, what needs me today. I wanted to pick up my\\nphone with coffee and see one glance before I even open the laptop.\\n\\nSo I set up a small scheduled job on my Mac. Each weekday morning it runs my agent\\nheadless with a self-contained prompt, and the agent pulls the real signals from my\\nactual projects: my site's numbers, the top task from my backlog, the status of the\\ncouple of GitHub PRs and issues I'm watching, and a quick triage of my last-24h\\ninbox. Then it emails me one short brief. It lands before I start, I read it\\nanywhere on my phone, and I know exactly where to dive in.\\n\\nThe friction was one thing, and it's the reason I'm writing this down. The agent\\ncould gather everything but couldn't send — Gmail kept returning \\\"Insufficient\\nscope,\\\" even though the tool clearly showed \\\"Always allow.\\\" That toggle is a tool\\npermission; it does not grant the Google OAuth scopes. The fix was to reconnect the\\nGmail connector and approve read + send on Google's own consent screen. Once the\\ntoken actually had the scopes, the brief sent — and now it arrives every workday.\\n\\n## Reproduce this\\nPrerequisites: an agent CLI you can run non-interactively\\n([Claude Code](https://www.anthropic.com/claude-code)) with a Gmail connector;\\n[`gh`](https://cli.github.com) for GitHub; your project(s) checked out locally; a\\nscheduler (macOS `launchd`; cron elsewhere).\\nYour agent will need from you: your Gmail address, the repos/sites to watch, and\\nwhat to include in the brief.\\nSteps:\\n1. Grant Gmail the real scopes. The gotcha: the \\\"Always allow\\\" tool-permission\\n   toggle is NOT the OAuth grant. Reconnect the Gmail connector (disconnect →\\n   reconnect) and approve read + send on Google's consent screen (`gmail.readonly`\\n   plus `gmail.modify`/send). Verify by having the agent read one thread and create\\n   a draft — if it says \\\"Insufficient scope,\\\" the token still lacks it.\\n2. Write a self-contained briefing prompt (the scheduled agent starts with no\\n   context): pull your numbers, the top item from your backlog file, `gh` status of\\n   the PRs/issues you watch, and a Gmail triage of the last ~24h; then send ONE\\n   short email to your own address. Degrade gracefully — a failing source is\\n   skipped, the email still sends.\\n3. Run it headless from a small script: `claude -p \\\"\u003cprompt\u003e\\\" --dangerously-skip-permissions`.\\n4. Schedule it: macOS `launchd` (`StartCalendarInterval`) on weekdays before you\\n   start — it runs on wake if the Mac was asleep. (cron on Linux.)\\n5. Test it now — a real email should land that you can open on your phone.\\nVerify: a short brief lands in your inbox each workday, with the sections you chose,\\nreadable on your phone before you open your laptop.\\n\",\n  \"after_you_apply_this\": \"Once you have actually applied this story's steps to the user's own task, close the loop: call report_reproduction with this slug and an HONEST result — 'worked', 'partial' (you produced the result but the user hasn't verified it yet), or 'failed'. This is how a story's reproduction count reflects reality. Never report a story you did not apply.\"\n}"}}}
