{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"15bcb20f-93ad-4ae5-ac49-63d5b43ce946","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have investigated the reasons behind the silent failure of your nightly launchd job and applied fixes to the relevant files. The root causes and remedies have been documented in [`ANSWER.md`](file:///private/tmp/h-JYkwBh/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Causes \u0026 Fixes\n\n1. **Missing `USER` in launchd environment**:\n   - **Cause:** macOS `launchd` does not populate standard shell environment variables like `USER`. Without `USER`, Claude Code could not locate credentials in keychain storage, exiting immediately with `Not logged in · Please run /login`.\n   - **Fix:** Added `USER` (`vk`) to `EnvironmentVariables` in [`Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`](file:///private/tmp/h-JYkwBh/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist#L24-L28).\n\n2. **Zsh read-only variable assignment (`status=$?`)**:\n   - **Cause:** In zsh, `status` is a read-only alias for `$?`. Attempting to assign `status=$?` killed `bin/nightly-review.zsh` immediately, right between the failing agent command and the failure notification call—completely silencing the reporter.\n   - **Fix:** Replaced `status` with `rc` in [`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///private/tmp/h-JYkwBh/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18-L24).\n\n3. **Multi-line prompt argument under headless launchd**:\n   - **Cause:** Passing multi-line prompt arguments into headless CLI sessions under launchd is prone to argument/input truncation or waiting on stdin.\n   - **Fix:** Piped the prompt via stdin (`print -r -- \"$PROMPT\" | claude -p ...`) in [`bin/nightly-review.zsh`](file:///private/tmp/h-JYkwBh/bin/nightly-review.zsh#L18).\n\n4. **Notifier relying on locked Keychain without reading config**:\n   - **Cause:** [`bin/notify.sh`](file:///private/tmp/h-JYkwBh/bin/notify.sh) queried the macOS keychain directly via `security find-generic-password -s tg-bot -w`, which fails when the machine is unattended/locked at 02:30. The fallback configuration in [`.config/nightly-review/config.toml`](file:///private/tmp/h-JYkwBh/.config/nightly-review/config.toml) was never parsed.\n   - **Fix:** Updated [`bin/notify.sh`](file:///private/tmp/h-JYkwBh/bin/notify.sh) to read `telegram_bot_token` and `chat_id` from `config.toml`, falling back to `security` only if not present.\n","duration_seconds":150.422827,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":242369,"output_tokens":4566,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":576850,"total_tokens":246935}}}
